# CLARITY frontend — copy to `.env` (never commit `.env`)
#
# === Go live locally (real Supabase auth) ===
# 1. Open https://supabase.com → your project → Project Settings → API
# 2. Paste:
#      VITE_SUPABASE_URL      = Project URL
#      VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = anon public key
# 3. Keep VITE_API_BASE_URL pointing at local FastAPI
# 4. Keep VITE_AUTH_BYPASS=false so login/register use the backend
# 5. Apply SQL migrations 001 → 003 in the Supabase SQL Editor
#    (see docs/go-live-locally.md)
#
# === Demo escape hatch ===
# Set VITE_AUTH_BYPASS=true (or omit in `npm run dev`) to explore the UI
# without Supabase. Demo mode can still poll GitHub activity when
# VITE_API_BASE_URL is set and backend APP_ENV=development.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=PASTE_ANON_PUBLIC_KEY_HERE
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/v1
VITE_AUTH_BYPASS=false
